SUMMARY:Roaming Readers: A Walking Audiobook Club!
DESCRIPTION:Join us as we walk the trails of RTP while listening to 
 audiobooks! After\, feel free to join us at Drift Coffee Shop & Kitchen RTP 
 for an optional discussion about the book and a chance to meet new 
 people.\n\n \n\nThis month’s suggested audiobook is Altered Carbon by 
 Richard K Morgan (available on Hoopla). If you have already read it\, or 
 would prefer another title\, we suggest: Of Monsters and Mainframes by 
 Barbara Truelove (available on Hoopla) or Area X by Jeff Vandermeer 
 (limited copies available on Libby). \n\n \n\nThis event is for book 
 lovers\, the book-curious\, people who haven’t been able to make time to 
 read (or listen) for fun\, introverts\, extroverts\, exercisers\, 
 caregivers pushing strollers\, (leashed) dog owners\, groups\, singles\, 
 nature lovers\, and multi-taskers!\n\n \n\nAll paces welcome\, please take 
 breaks when you need them. We know it is easy to get transported to another 
 world when listening to your book. Be sure to stay alert as we will be 
 crossing roads and may encounter uneven pavement. \n\n \n\nWhile attendance 
 is free\, please register here to receive reminders and stay in the know 
 for any updates. Free public parking is located on the deck just across the 
 street at 3150 Elion Drive. We will meet at 3151 Elion Drive Durham\, NC 
 27713.\n\n \n\nQuestions? Email Elle at kfarmer@dconc.gov.
LOCATION:Offsite
ORGANIZER;CN="Elle F.":MAILTO:kfarmer@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Book Club, Health & Fitness, Social
UID:LibCal-14288-16608439
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16608439
END:VEVENT
