SUMMARY:Adult Story Time -- I'll Mature When I'm Dead
DESCRIPTION:Read-alouds are for grown-ups too! Join us for a weekday 
 evening adult story time at the North Regional Library. Flop on the carpet 
 with a floor pillow\, pull up a chair\, or sit at a table if you want to 
 bring your own dinner or snacks. Spend an hour listening to read-alouds 
 from books and stories in the library collection. Tea\, coffee\, and hot 
 chocolate will be provided.\n\nThis month: I'll Mature When I'm Dead. In 
 this collection of essays\, humorist Dave Barry takes on self-image\, the 
 battle of the sexes\, celebrityhood\, technology\, parenting styles\, 
 certain unmentionable medical procedures\, and many other topics of 
 adulthood. If you are like many adults and have struggled hard against 
 growing up\, you will very likely appreciate this month's read-aloud 
 selections.\n\nRegistration is appreciated but not required.\n\nE-mail Bob 
 with any questions: rskesler@dconc.gov
LOCATION:North Meeting Room - Full Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Bob S.":MAILTO:rskesler@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Literacy, Story Time
