BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260921T220000Z
DTEND:20260921T233000Z
DTSTAMP:20260921T000000Z
SUMMARY:Starting Smart: Understanding NC Business Regulations and Requirements
DESCRIPTION:Presented by the Economic Development Partnership of 
 NC\n\nDon’t let confusing rules or mixed messages hold you back! This 
 workshop cuts through the noise and gives you the straight facts about what 
 it takes to launch your business the right way.\n\n We’ll walk you 
 through the state\, local\, and federal requirements and point you to free 
 resources North Carolina offers to help you succeed.\n\n Get answers to the 
 questions every new entrepreneur asks:\n\n\n	I have an EIN… now 
 what?\n	DBA\, LLC\, Corporation\, S-Corp - what’s the difference?\n	How 
 much does it cost\, and how long will it take?\n	Do I need a license or a 
 State Tax Number?\n	Can I run my business from home?\n\n\n Leave with 
 clarity\, confidence\, and a roadmap to turn your idea into a real 
 business.\n\n \n\nSharon Walker is a Senior Small Business Advisor with 
 EDPNC. She is a business consultant with almost 30 years of experience in 
 customer service\, technical support\, and project management. Prior to 
 coming to EDPNC\, she has worked with DHHS and NCDOR\, along with large 
 corporations\, Kodak and MCI/WorldCom. Outside of work\, Sharon volunteers 
 with an international educational 501c(3) organization and has served as 
 treasurer and instructor for the local chapter for more than 10 years. 
 Sharon is also a seamstress and costumer with over 30 years of experience 
 working with textiles.  \n\n
ORGANIZER;CN="Austin Daniels":MAILTO:ausdaniels@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Business, Career Development
UID:LibCal-14288-17344068
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17344068
END:VEVENT
