SUMMARY:Duke Ballet & Books
DESCRIPTION:Duke Ballet & Books is a group of Duke University student 
 volunteers who run free arts and literacy programming for 6-9 year 
 olds.\n\nThere are two parts to every Ballet & Books session:\n\n1. 
 45-minute ballet class where students learn choreography to perform at an 
 end-of-semester showcase.\n2. 45-minute reading mentorship session where 
 mentors and students read together and do related activities aimed at 
 helping build literacy skills.\n\nTo learn more and register\, contact 
 duke@balletandbooks.org\n
LOCATION:Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Christina Economou":MAILTO:ceconomou@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Literacy
UID:LibCal-14288-17325508
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17325508
END:VEVENT
