SUMMARY:Women in G.L.A.M. featuring Black Voices in Galleries\, Libraries\, Archives\, & Museums
DESCRIPTION:\na {\n    text-decoration: none\;\n    color: #464feb\;\n}\ntr 
 th\, tr td {\n    border: 1px solid #e6e6e6\;\n}\ntr th {\n    
 background-color: #f5f5f5\;\n}\n\nPresented by Leola Curatorial\, "Women in 
 G.L.A.M." is an intergenerational and cross-disciplinary public 
 conversation centering the experiences\, contributions\, and leadership of 
 women of color working across galleries\, libraries\, archives\, and 
 museums. This event brings together cultural workers to discuss the 
 realities of building careers within the institutions responsible for 
 preserving\, interpreting\, and sharing our collective histories.\n\nPlease 
 register here: Women in G.L.A.M: Careers in Galleries\, Libraries\, 
 Archives\, and Museums. Tickets\, Saturday\, Septem…
LOCATION:Main Auditorium\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Natalie Killion":MAILTO:nkillion@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts, Business, Career Development, Durham
