DTSTART:20261007T150000Z
DTEND:20261007T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20261007T000000Z
SUMMARY:Touch-a-Truck with The City of Durham Fire Department
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for an exciting Touch-a-Truck event with the 
 City of Durham Fire Department! Kids and families can explore the fire 
 truck up close\, meet the firefighters\, and learn valuable fire safety 
 tips. This is in observance of National Fire Prevention Week\, which is 
 from October 4-10\, 2026. This year’s campaign focuses on the everyday 
 charging habits that can help reduce the risk of lithium-ion battery fires 
 and keep homes and communities safer.\n\nThis program will be held at 
 11a.m. directly after our 10:30 firefighter-themed storytime. \n\nPlease 
 note: The Firefighters will be on duty and if they receive an emergency 
 call\, they could be late or may not be able to come at all.\n\nQuestions? 
 Accessibility questions? Accommodation needs?  Please email Molly at 
 mschaefer@dconc.gov or call 919-560-0236.  We ask that all requests be made 
 at least three (3) business days prior to the event to ensure we can 
 provide the best accommodations possible! Thank you!
LOCATION:North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Molly Schaefer":MAILTO:mschaefer@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Durham
UID:LibCal-14288-17452537
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17452537
