BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261009T140000Z
DTEND:20261009T150000Z
DTSTAMP:20261009T000000Z
SUMMARY:Memory Cafe
DESCRIPTION:Come join us for a monthly activity for people with dementia 
 and their caregivers. Memory Cafes host activities designed to engage in 
 the present\, without the expectations of using short-term memory or 
 forward thinking. This month\, we will be talking about emotions. We'll 
 make large paintings based on emotions using different painting techniques 
 (finger-painting\, brushes\, stamping\, etc.) Come ready to get messy. 
 Weather permitting\, we'll be outside for this program. \n\nThis program 
 will be held on October 9\, 2026\, at 10 a.m. at the North Regional Library 
 in the small programming room or outside. The address is 221 Milton 
 Rd.\n\nIf you have any accessibility questions or accommodation needs\, 
 please contact me at dpeterson@dconc.gov. We ask that all requests be made 
 at least three (3) business days prior to the event to ensure we can 
 provide the best accommodations possible! Please email me if you plan to 
 attend and have nut allergies so that we can make accommodations.
LOCATION:North Regional - Children's Programming Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Desiree Peterson":MAILTO:dpeterson@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Low Sensory Stimulation, Summer Reading
UID:LibCal-14288-17207256
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17207256
END:VEVENT
