DTEND:20261010T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20261010T000000Z
SUMMARY:Outing in Duke Gardens
DESCRIPTION:One Walk to Rule Them All\, One Path to Find Them\,\nOne Garden 
 to Bring Them All — and in the beauty bind them:\nAn Outing in Duke 
 Gardens.\n\nRain or Shine! \n\nSarah P. Duke Gardens\n\n420 Anderson St\, 
 Durham\, NC \n\nCheck in any time between 10 a.m. and 12 p.m.!\n\nJoin us 
 at Sarah P. Duke Gardens\, where winding paths and breathtaking blooms 
 await beneath the open sky.  We’ll meet you at the Rollins Plaza in front 
 of the Barnes Welcome Center at the benches close to the Gardens Café. 
 After checking in you’ll be free to explore the splendor of the gardens 
 on foot\, whether in fellowship or in solitary ramble. Be sure to keep 
 track of your minutes on your One Walk to Rule Them All exercise tracker! 
 Check in and sign up for extra entries into the grand prize raffle will be 
 available from 10 a.m. to 12 p.m. (you must return a completed One Walk to 
 Rule Them All tracker by December 10th to be eligible for extra 
 entries)\n\nRegistration is required. Children must be accompanied by an 
 adult. This program is made possible through the generosity of the Friends 
 of the Durham Library and in partnership with Duke Gardens. For questions 
 about this event\, please contact Jessica\, jllundin@dconc.gov. \n\nAll 
 participants must abide by Sarah P. Duke Gardens policies and visitation 
 guidelines. You can also access a map of the gardens online.\n\nParking 
 Information: Public parking at the welcome center is managed by Duke 
 Parking & Transportation and available first come\, first served at 
 $2/hour. You can also walk\, take the bus\, or bike to the 
 Gardens.\n\nClick here for hours and directions. \n\nClick here for 
 accessibility information.\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n
LOCATION:Offsite
ORGANIZER;CN="Jessica L.":MAILTO:jllundin@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Friends of the Durham Library, Health & Fitness, One Walk
