SUMMARY:Opioid Overdose Prevention and Response Training
DESCRIPTION:Join us at South Regional for an opioid overdose prevention and 
 response training from Durham County Public Health!\n\nYou'll 
 learn:\n\n\n	About the philosophy and practice of reducing the negative 
 health and social outcomes associated with drug use\n	How to recognize an 
 overdose\n	How to respond to and reverse an overdose using nasal naloxone 
 (Narcan)\n	And more!\n\n\nAttendees will receive a free naloxone 
 kit!\n\nDid you know there are multiple FREE nasal naloxone vending 
 machines located around Durham that are accessible 24/7? Visit Durham 
 County Public Health website for more information.\n\n\n\n\n
LOCATION:South Meeting Room\, South Regional Library (4505 S. Alston Ave)
ORGANIZER;CN="Elle F.":MAILTO:kfarmer@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Classes & Lectures, Health & Fitness, One Walk
