SUMMARY:Why are Katmai's bears so fat? [in person only]
DESCRIPTION:This event registration is for the in-person event ONLY. 
 \n\nFor the virtual event\, please visit: 
 https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17616246\n\n\nFat Bear Week 
 devotees\, assemble! \n\nJoin us for a live (virtual) program with a Katmai 
 National Park and Preserve ranger to learn about the ecosystem of the 
 Brooks River inside Alaska's Katmai National Park and Preserve. This 
 mile-long stretch of water supports sockeye salmon\, a keystone species. 
 These fish are the secret to the success for not only the birds and mammals 
 that call this area home\, but also the trees and plants along the 
 riverbank. \n\nThe ranger will talk about the ecosystem and take questions 
 for about 30 minutes. Afterward\, stay for more bear learning and 
 crafts!\n\nThis program will be in the 3rd floor Innovation Lab and is 
 geared toward tweens and older\, but younger patrons are welcome too! Best 
 for elementary-age and up.\n\n \n\nIf you have any accessibility questions 
 or accommodation needs\, please contact us at Maker_STEAM@dconc.gov. We ask 
 that all requests be made at least 2 business days prior to the event to 
 ensure we can provide the best accommodations possible.
